                     <textLang mainLang="ang">Old English</textLang>
                     <msItem>
                        <title>Blank leaf of a gospel book, containing added documents in Old
                           English</title>
                     </msItem>
                  </msContents>
                  <history>
                     <origin>
                        <origDate calendar="#gregorian" notBefore="0980" notAfter="0999">s. x
                           ex</origDate>
                     </origin>
                     <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_190">Ely,
                           Cambridgeshire, Benedictine abbey and (1109) cathedral priory of St Peter
                           and St Etheldreda</orgName><p>An Ely attribution was initially accepted
                           in MLGB2 (1964), p. 78. The corresponding MLGB index card provided the
                           following information in support of the attribution: 'Two Ely documents,
                           one of which begins "Her is on þysse crystes bec". Probably once part of
                           C.U.L. KK.1.24 from which Tib B.v fol. 76 (containing a probable Ely
                           document) certainly comes.' However, the Supplement (1987), p. 35
                           rejected the Ely attribution for Tiberius B.v fol. 76 and Cambridge,
                           University Library, MS KK.1.24 on the basis that the documents related
                           instead to Ramsey abbey. The Supplement did not change the status of
                           folio 74 to rejected, but this seems to have been an accidental
                           omission.</p></provenance>
                  </history>
               </msPart>
