                     <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_190">Ely,
                           Cambridgeshire, Benedictine abbey and (1109) cathedral priory of St Peter
                           and St Etheldreda</orgName><p>An Ely attribution was initially accepted
                           in MLGB2 (1964), p. 78, albeit with a question mark. The corresponding
                           MLGB index card recorded the following evidence to support the
                           attribution: 'Formerly part of Cambridge University Library, MS Kk.1.24.
                           Contains document relating to Hatfield, Herts CLA ii no. 138.' However,
                           the Supplement (1987), p. 35 rejected the Ely attribution on the basis
                           that the documents related instead to Ramsey abbey.</p></provenance>
